  "response_text": "To allocate new stacks, we need to ensure that we avoid the main stack or heap memory region. We can do this by taking the MSP and subtracting the main stack size. From now on, we\u2019re assuming we\u2019ve already offset the address to avoid the main stack\u2019s memory space. Since we know how many stacks we want, we\u2019ll call it N, we can calculate the offset needed in memory to access a stack by multiplying the stack\u2019s index by the set stack size. As for assigning these stacks to threads, we can hand each thread an index number from 0 to N during creation and all it has to do is perform the calculation above to access its stack.\\n",
